face-image: img/redfront.jpg

= May Day, 1929

Tensions are at a boiling point across Berlin. The central committee and the Rotfrontkämpferbund (RFB) are preparing massive May Day rallies across the city. 

However, the SPD-controlled Prussian Interior Ministry and Police President Otto Zörgiebel view our preparations with extreme hostility. How we approach the demonstration depends heavily on our current relations with the Social Democrats and their state apparatus.

- @defy_ban: Prepare for direct street defiance regardless of police orders.
- @peaceful_march: Keep the marches peaceful and strictly contained to working-class districts.
- @joint_rally: Invite SPD workers and trade unionists to join a unified red May Day march.
- @easy_discard


@defy_ban
// Triggers Blutmai if SPD relations are low to moderate (< 50)
go-to: blutmai_erupts if spd_relation < 50; peaceful_perm if spd_relation >= 50

@blutmai_erupts
on-arrival: blutmai = 1; spd_relation -= 20; z_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; workers_kpd += 4; unemployed_kpd += 4; strife += 1; rfb_banned = 1; rfb_strength -= 50; left_dissent += 3; center_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent += 3; neorevisionist_dissent += 3; labor_strength -= 3
face-image: img/blutmai.jpg

Zörgiebel and the SPD police ministry issued an outright ban on all outdoor demonstrations. When thousands of our workers took to the streets in Neukölln and Wedding anyway, the police responded with extreme violence, using live ammunition and armored cars. 

Dozens of workers and innocent bystanders lie dead. In the aftermath, the SPD government officially bans our paramilitary wing, the RFKB (*Rotfrontkämpferbund*). 

Our party press decries the incident as *Blutmai*—Bloody May. Fury sweeps through our membership, devastating the Conciliator faction's push for cooperation and severely damaging relations with Social Democracy.

- @blame_zorgiebel: Direct all outrage toward Zörgiebel and the SPD leadership as "social-fascist bloodhounds."
- @appeal_rank_and_file: Focus our rhetoric on winning over horrified SPD rank-and-file workers against their leaders.

@blame_zorgiebel
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 10; center_strength += 5; center_dissent -= 5; comintern_approval += 5

We double down on the Comintern line: Zörgiebel's bullets prove that Social Democracy is merely the left wing of fascism. The Zentralkomitee hardens its stance against any reconciliation.

@appeal_rank_and_file
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5; labor_strength += 3; center_dissent += 3; comintern_approval -= 5

We explicitly distinguish between the reactionary SPD police chiefs and the SPD rank-and-file workers, calling on ordinary trade unionists to join us in condemning the police violence.


@peaceful_perm
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5; workers_kpd += 3; unemployed_kpd += 3

Because our relations with the Social Democratic government have improved, the police ban is quietly relaxed for designated routes. The demonstration proceeds peacefully under the watchful eyes of the authorities, showcasing the discipline of the communist vanguard.


@peaceful_march
view-if: spd_relation >= 30
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5; workers_kpd += 3; unemployed_kpd += 3; rfb_militancy -= 0.05

We instruct our local cells and the RFB to avoid provocative confrontations and maintain strict discipline. The marches proceed through working-class quarters without major bloodshed. While the SPD police remain tense, disaster is averted, and onlookers respect our restraint.


@joint_rally
choose-if: spd_relation >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD and their trade unions do not trust us enough to march together (Requires SPD Relation >= 45).
on-arrival: spd_relation += 15; workers_kpd += 5; unemployed_kpd += 5; workers_spd += 3; communist_coalition += 2; rfb_strength += 50; rfb_militancy += 0.05; z_relation -= 8; dvp_relation -= 8
achievement: die_rote_fahne

Leveraging our high standing with Social Democratic workers and left-wing SPD executives, we successfully organize a joint May Day rally. 

Red flags and Reichsbanner banners march side-by-side through Berlin. This powerful display of proletarian unity inspires working-class neighborhoods and sends shockwaves through the bourgeois parties and right-wing paramilitaries, who view the emerging United Front with terror.